# Who is responsible for which files.
#
# With a single maintainer and no required approvals, this file documents
# responsibility; it does not enforce a second review. The explicit entries
# mark the files that decide what runs on developer machines and in CI, what
# gets published, how leaked data is found and what the project promises.
# They stay with the maintainers even if the default rule changes. Later
# rules take precedence.
* @ecclium/maintainers

/.github/ @ecclium/maintainers
/.vscode/ @ecclium/maintainers
/package.json @ecclium/maintainers
/packages/*/package.json @ecclium/maintainers
/pnpm-lock.yaml @ecclium/maintainers
/pnpm-workspace.yaml @ecclium/maintainers
/mise.toml @ecclium/maintainers
/mise.compat.toml @ecclium/maintainers
/mise.lock @ecclium/maintainers
/mise.compat.lock @ecclium/maintainers
/.gitleaks.toml @ecclium/maintainers
/lefthook.yml @ecclium/maintainers
/.gitignore @ecclium/maintainers
/.gitattributes @ecclium/maintainers
/brand/ @ecclium/maintainers
/docs/adr/ @ecclium/maintainers
/SECURITY.md @ecclium/maintainers
/PROMISE.md @ecclium/maintainers
/LICENSE @ecclium/maintainers
/NOTICE @ecclium/maintainers
